From 70fb730a7b2068fb8116a8560faa567c4cffb654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:51:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] newuoa: use level-3 BLAS for the shift of XBASE for n
 >= 100

With an external BLAS/LAPACK and n >= 100, do the whole O(n^3) shift of
XBASE with level-2/3 BLAS: the per-point rank-two and rank-one updates
of the lower triangle of BMAT(NPT+1:,:) become one DSYR2K and two DSYRK,
the per-column products with ZMAT (DGEMV and DGER until now) two DGEMMs,
and the updates of GQ and HQ DSPMV and DSPR2.  This needs about 5n^2
doubles of workspace, allocated for each shift; if that fails, for
smaller n, and without an external BLAS, the original loops are used.
DSYRK, DSYR2K, DSPMV and DSPR2 are added to the routines required from
an external BLAS.  The new function is kept out of line (with GCC and
compatible compilers): inlined into NEWUOB, it made some runs with
n = 50, which do not use it, up to 6% slower.

The summation order changes, so results differ in the last bits for
n >= 100.  With a cheap objective, the time per evaluation drops by
another 1.03-1.10x (n = 100) to 1.17-1.22x (n = 200) with
single-threaded OpenBLAS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
